{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf","id":1508026,"title":"Can a Fomor be near identical to a werewolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-11T06:37:53-07:00","id":1508026,"title":"Can a Fomor be near identical to a werewolf?","content":"Taking the right powers ( and mabye Taints, Merits and Flaws too? ) from Freak Legion and Possessed: a player's guide, could it be possible to create a fomor who's powers , weaknesses and appearance are virtually identical to a werewolf?<br /> <br /> Here's my attempt:<br /> <br /> POWERS<br /> <br /> * Shapechange - one alternate form ( werewolf ). The problem here is <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> these new shapes are always a corrupted version of the natural animal or person: mangy, misshapen and Wyrm-maddened </div> </div> </div>. Basically the Fomor would resemble a Black Spiral Dancer. I've yet to find a way to disguise this problem.<br /> * Immunity to Delirium - as any Garou<br /> * Berserk - for a Rage score.<br /> * Spirit Ties - for a Gnosis score.<br /> * Umbral Passage - to step sideways like a Garou.<br /> * Size, Claws, Fangs, Enhanced Strength / Stamina - for the alternate form.<br /> * Sense the Unnatural - like the Garou gift of the same name.<br /> * Regeneration - to recover like a Garou, but it causes tumor growth so I guess it requires as secondary power Immunity ( cancer )<br /> * Garou Gifts - from Freak Legion, as many as needed<br /> * Deception - to mask the taint of Wyrm<br /> * Horror - to induce Delirium as a Garou<br /> * Triatic Scant - to smell like a Garou<br /> <br /> <br /> TAINTS<br /> <br /> * Severe allergy ( silver )<br /> * Addiction - shapechange, once per full moon<br /> <br /> Mabye the Merit - Hidden Power could be used to disguise the mangy / misshapen appearance of the alternate form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 04-11-2023, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T09:55:45-07:00","id":1508045,"title":"","content":"With Formor, you really have a license to do whatever you want. You even have a good license to create &quot;werewolves&quot; like those from folklore or pop culture, IE they're worgs or spread the condition via bites. <br /> <br /> I would er with a side of caution when it comes to lab-made monstrosities: if they can get it right without significant issues, it'll get a lot of attention and mass production will be in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T10:44:05-07:00","id":1508051,"title":"","content":"Can a Fomor be identical to a Fera/werewolf? I don't see why not, like you said there is enough powers and merits/flaws to make something very close if not functionally the same. My understanding is that the Gaian possessed, which I believe are called Kami but I don't recall, are often like pseudo-fera anyways though I also could me mistaken about that. Plus we already have all the Mockery Breeds and really if you think about it those are basically Fomor Shifters that were able to breed out so there can be a case made for such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T11:20:31-07:00","id":1508057,"title":"","content":"There's also a power in freaks legion that allows the fomori to &quot;reproduce&quot; and turn others or their offspring into the same kind of fomor.<br /> <br /> Between that and the tendency of fomori families to develope spirit rites, it really makes you wonder if the origin of the garou are really as &quot;Gaian&quot; as they believe....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 04-11-2023, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T14:46:32-07:00","id":1508077,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not particularly gifted with the mechanical side of things, but from the theoretical or conceptual level, I don\u2019t see anything particular infeasible about a fomori resembling a werewolf, particularly the werewolf of popular culture or of folklore, although individual STs may have their own reasons for not wanting to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T15:59:47-07:00","id":1508080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf#post1508026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the right powers ( and mabye Taints, Merits and Flaws too? ) from Freak Legion and Possessed: a player's guide, could it be possible to create a fomor who's powers , weaknesses and appearance are virtually identical to a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ultimate question here though, is who are you trying to deceive?<br /> <br /> No matter how close you make their stats, spirits and spiritual aware characters (most Garou and Fera, some mages, some Wan-Kuei even) are easily going to spot the difference between spirit-possession and the more fully integrated half-flesh/half-spirit nature of the Garou. There's a ton of low level stuff out there that is going to if not instantly see through this, at least very easily pick up that something is wrong and needs investigating.<br /> <br /> If you want to try to fool some Lost Cubs and lure them to the Wyrm? Seems a bit overkill, but sure. Want a decoy to fool the local Garou about where your BSD allies are? Works well enough. Want to use them to wage attrition warfare by forcing the Garou to cover up rampages to avoid breaching the Veil? Well then you're just trying to trick humans, so yeah that's easy enough.<br /> <br /> The goal here is certainly going to matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508051#post1508051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Fomor be identical to a Fera/werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they can't be truly identical because they're entirely different things on a spiritual level. Fooling those that can't sense those differences is easy though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My understanding is that the Gaian possessed, which I believe are called Kami but I don't recall, are often like pseudo-fera anyways though I also could me mistaken about that. </div> </div> </div>You have the names right, but this is very far from how the Kami operate. Kami are the most deliberately chosen/designed of the Possessed, and each is given a specific mission from Gaia (though these can be tasks that can take multiple human life spans to achieve, or aren't even things that can be achieved, just maintained until someone else has to take over). They're also the least restricted in their base forms, as Gaia can make Kami out of any natural thing; not just animals, but even non-living environmental features.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus we already have all the Mockery Breeds and really if you think about it those are basically Fomor Shifters that were able to breed out so there can be a case made for such a thing. </div> </div> </div>They're something different, and as Conradine ran into, have a lot of tells that they're not what they seem to be to those that know the Garou and Fera. They're not designed to be infiltrators, but higher powered servants of the Wyrm's cause than most Formori manage to be.<br /> <br /> Again, if you're trying to force the Garou to spend resources covering up some War Wolves going nuts in public? Humans aren't going to know the difference. Spiritually aware supernaturals are going to easily know they're tainted things different from what they're copying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508057#post1508057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between that and the tendency of fomori families to develope spirit rites, it really makes you wonder if the origin of the garou are really as &quot;Gaian&quot; as they believe....</div> </div> </div> </div>Not... really? It would take very little for Gaia to have turned a few Kami into the shifters by tweaking things a bit to get Kami that can make more of themselves by having kids (and this matches the sense that they have a Gaia - or other high level spirit - ordained duty/purpose).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T17:16:34-07:00","id":1508087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508080#post1508080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not... really? It would take very little for Gaia to have turned a few Kami into the shifters by tweaking things a bit to get Kami that can make more of themselves by having kids (and this matches the sense that they have a Gaia - or other high level spirit - ordained duty/purpose).</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, you're no fun. Where's your sense of conspiracy?<br /> <br /> It's still hilarious that from a mechanical perspective, Fomori are the only possessed capable of reproducing directly. Doubly hilarious when you realize there's a Gorgon breed who's entire shtick is supposed to be <i>Just That</i>, but they lack that specific power mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T17:30:51-07:00","id":1508090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508080#post1508080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ultimate question here though, is who are you trying to deceive?<br /> <br /> No matter how close you make their stats, spirits and spiritual aware characters (most Garou and Fera, some mages, some Wan-Kuei even) are easily going to spot the difference between spirit-possession and the more fully integrated half-flesh/half-spirit nature of the Garou. There's a ton of low level stuff out there that is going to if not instantly see through this, at least very easily pick up that something is wrong and needs investigating.<br /> <br /> If you want to try to fool some Lost Cubs and lure them to the Wyrm? Seems a bit overkill, but sure. Want a decoy to fool the local Garou about where your BSD allies are? Works well enough. Want to use them to wage attrition warfare by forcing the Garou to cover up rampages to avoid breaching the Veil? Well then you're just trying to trick humans, so yeah that's easy enough.<br /> <br /> The goal here is certainly going to matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they could be a Kinfolk that were bullied be they Garou parents and this was a propose of the Wyrm to give then power to fight back turned in something that resemblence a Garou, in that case they would be visually similar for the purpose of humiliation.<br /> <br /> I know that already have the Skindancers, but it is something to think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:17:33-07:00","id":1508095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508087#post1508087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's your sense of conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well murdered by society before I even know what it was.<br /> <br /> Appeal to my sense of mystery if you want me to react more happily to such things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508090#post1508090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they could be a Kinfolk that were bullied be they Garou parents and this was a propose of the Wyrm to give then power to fight back turned in something that resemblence a Garou, in that case they would be visually similar for the purpose of humiliation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... OK... but beyond provoking a Frenzy check with humiliation (which would be just as bad if the kin willingly became a standard fomori-type), ultimately you're taking the effort and building up an extremely powerful fomor... that's basically a match for a starting level Garou of similar combat experience and is going to get wrecked by some decent low level powers.<br /> <br /> And it's easy enough for the Garou to figure out how it happened, so the &quot;looks like a werewolf&quot; rubbing the salt in the wound is of minimal impact compared to the rest of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:32:11-07:00","id":1508097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508090#post1508090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that already have the Skindancers, but it is something to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know for sure that skindancers Aren't an exotic type of Fomori? As demonstrated, making a functional werewolf using fomori powers isn't hard.<br /> <br /> In play, nothing would really be tangibly different if the banes hide their scent and don't raise a fuss. It'd also make a fitting wyrm plot, release a ritual that allows kinfolk to become &quot;Werewolves&quot; at the cost of the garou, have the ritual work &quot;perfectly&quot; at first and spread out, and after their population reaches a typing point, release the banes to cause havok. The chaos would be a feast for the wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:35:20-07:00","id":1508099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf#post1508026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem here is . Basically the Fomor would resemble a Black Spiral Dancer. I've yet to find a way to disguise this problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fomori powers are not meant to be limiting. Books usually encourage the ST to create whatever new fomori powers they need, or to change the flavor text of existing powers as needed. So in terms of mechanics, as long as you are willing to add a whole lot of fomori powers on this fomori, you should be able to have a creature that will appear to be a Garou to other beings in the setting.<br /> <br /> I think the real question is what real narrative need is there in the game to have a fomori breed that is almost identical to a Garou?<br /> <br /> We already have the Black Spiral Dancers plus loads of other corrupted Garou who serve the Wyrm in some capacity. You can do any plot with them that you would with any fomori breed that could appear to be a Garou. (Now if you intended to emulate other kinds of werewolf depictions that don't match the Garou, then I could see the benefit of it.)<br /> <br /> If you are going to invest the time to create a new fomori breed, it should be to allow you, as the ST, to do something new that you could not previously do before. Provide a new experience for your PCs. Otherwise this just appears to be a process of trying to be clever just to be clever.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:36:28-07:00","id":1508100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508097#post1508097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we know for sure that skindancers Aren't an exotic type of Fomori? As demonstrated, making a functional werewolf using fomori powers isn't hard.<br /> <br /> In play, nothing would really be tangibly different if the banes hide their scent and don't raise a fuss. It'd also make a fitting wyrm plot, release a ritual that allows kinfolk to become &quot;Werewolves&quot; at the cost of the garou, have the ritual work &quot;perfectly&quot; at first and spread out, and after their population reaches a typing point, release the banes to cause havok. The chaos would be a feast for the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we know, because we're told out of character. Also, making a fomori with all of the stuff that Garou get takes so many power points that you'll either have very little Autonomy left, or you'll have a bunch of extra Taints that spoils the effect. It's not perfect, or even really functional, by any means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T07:26:50-07:00","id":1508153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508100#post1508100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, we know, because we're told out of character. Also, making a fomori with all of the stuff that Garou get takes so many power points that you'll either have very little Autonomy left, or you'll have a bunch of extra Taints that spoils the effect. It's not perfect, or even really functional, by any means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the point of the &quot;more powerful possessed&quot; sidebar.<br /> <br /> Possessed's rules assume everyone is being possessed by the same level of gaffling. The book explicitely points out that the rules can't apply to all types of possession and that NPCs being given way more or way less points with less autonomy loss is valid and expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T13:08:11-07:00","id":1508182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508153#post1508153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats the point of the &quot;more powerful possessed&quot; sidebar.<br /> <br /> Possessed's rules assume everyone is being possessed by the same level of gaffling. The book explicitely points out that the rules can't apply to all types of possession and that NPCs being given way more or way less points with less autonomy loss is valid and expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still doesn't make a dent on &quot;we are told out of character that Skindancers are not fomori&quot;. And just re-engineering Garou with fomori seems like both a narrative waste of time and effort and something that the banes in question might not be capable of accomplishing beyond the most surface-level faking, as they are still bound by their nature as banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T15:55:10-07:00","id":1508203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508182#post1508182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That still doesn't make a dent on &quot;we are told out of character that Skindancers are not fomori&quot;. And just re-engineering Garou with fomori seems like both a narrative waste of time and effort and something that the banes in question might not be capable of accomplishing beyond the most surface-level faking, as they are still bound by their nature as banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearification: Not trying to legit &quot;prove&quot; that skindancers were always fomori. Not trying to &quot;prove&quot; that werewolves were always fomori. I'm throwing around story ideas that sound cool.<br /> <br /> Seriously, are we not allowed to be creative with the rules or setting here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:37:51-07:00","id":1508209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508203#post1508203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clearification: Not trying to legit &quot;prove&quot; that skindancers were always fomori. Not trying to &quot;prove&quot; that werewolves were always fomori. I'm throwing around story ideas that sound cool.<br /> <br /> Seriously, are we not allowed to be creative with the rules or setting here?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one corner where it might not actually pay off, since W:tA is not meant to have some kind of ironic twist on the origin of the Garou. That's clever in the same way that Exalted 2nd edition was &quot;clever&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T16:43:58-07:00","id":1508211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1508203#post1508203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearification: Not trying to legit &quot;prove&quot; that skindancers were always fomori. Not trying to &quot;prove&quot; that werewolves were always fomori. I'm throwing around story ideas that sound cool.<br /> Seriously, are we not allowed to be creative with the rules or setting here?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you do at your table is your own business. We are allowed to disagree with ideas that are counter to the themes of the game or that we don't especially like, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T18:43:42-07:00","id":1508228,"title":"","content":"Also, a lot of threads where someone asks a question about how something works in the game end up with all sots of tangents about house-rules. While not necessarily something that gets to the level of threacrapping/derailing or anything, those of us that are trying to make sure the OP gets a clear answer about the state of the game are going to push back that creative alternate takes aren't something suggested in the books if that's the case; because we want to make sure what's the official answer and what isn't is clear to the OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T14:45:36-07:00","id":1508779,"title":"","content":"Not trying to go to far from the original topic, I also experimented creating a vampire.<br /> <br /> Fangs, addiction to blood, allergy to sun light, longevity and being able to contaminate others through bites... seems very much a possibility.<br /> <br /> From the lore perspective, it also could be arranged, IMO, to have the Beast as a representative of a court of blood / murder spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26085-raphaelrrcoelho","name":"raphaelrrcoelho","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T15:13:49-07:00","id":1508784,"title":"","content":"Officially, it's possible for the right Banes to possess a vampire as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T17:57:58-07:00","id":1508799,"title":"","content":"I will mention that the rules for Devil-Eaten (essentially Fomori with the serial numbers filed off so that they work with non-Werewolf cosmologies) in Mage's Book of Madness revised edition were specifically written so you could use them to create werewolves, as well as vampires, zombies, cyborgs, aliens, or whatever else you could think of. <br /> I think you could get a fair amount of mileage out of pseudo-werewolves and/or the idea of werewolves as a form of spiritual corruption, but I think that probably would work best in a Hunters Hunted game. (Or one of the witch hunter organizations like the Inquisition, Arcanum or Twilight agencies. It'd probably fit really well with the anime influences of Strike Force Zero.) And just as a matter of personal preference, I'd probably have them be limited to either the classic Lon Chaney Jr. Wolf Man appearance or the quadrupedal wolf beast from the climax of An American Werewolf in London. This is mostly just to preserve the Garou Crinos form as a specific Garou thing, and (in my own head at least) to represent that these pseudo werewolves are spiritually off, having only a single alternate form, and one that very obviously isn't the balanced half-man/half-wolf form of the Garou. <br /> Such is my opinion, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T03:41:54-07:00","id":1509359,"title":"","content":"Surprised no one has mentioned this yet; the &quot;Garou&quot; Fomori being horribly misshapen? Remind anyone of anything?<br /> <br /> They're posing as a Metis!<br /> <br /> Solves a lot of problems, creates a few others, but &quot;I'm a Metis with fucked up fur and a horrible skin condition&quot; saves you the effort of making a PERFECT Garou-imitation Fomor which honestly sounds like a lot more work than just hiring a Rank 1 BSD!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T08:28:00-07:00","id":1509378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508026-can-a-fomor-be-near-identical-to-a-werewolf?p=1509359#post1509359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised no one has mentioned this yet; the &quot;Garou&quot; Fomori being horribly misshapen? Remind anyone of anything?<br /> <br /> They're posing as a Metis!<br /> <br /> Solves a lot of problems, creates a few others, but &quot;I'm a Metis with fucked up fur and a horrible skin condition&quot; saves you the effort of making a PERFECT Garou-imitation Fomor which honestly sounds like a lot more work than just hiring a Rank 1 BSD!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess that Lunes could cut through that bullshit really quickly, since actual Garou have auspices, and a quick check in situations of genuine suspicion is to attempt an exorcism and ask questions later. If they're actual Garou, they won't be divided into a spirit and a rapidly-dying mortal being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}